#
# Emits the COMPLETE set-progress table for the CURRENT exercise slot, wrapped
# in a ``` code fence, exactly per workout-session/SKILL.md "(2) 세트 사이
# 진척도 표" format (owner-locked 2026-07-29, C10/C14/C17 2026-07-31):
#
#   <display>                                (header line 1)
#   ════...  (═ x 36, = set-grid width)      (header line 2, double rule)
#   부위: <primary> · 보조근 <secondary>      (header line 3, secondary optional)
#
#   [추세] 최근 <N>세션                        (trend block, >=1 session -- C10)
#    e1RM <sparkline> <latest>kg
#    VOL  <sparkline> <latest>kg
#
#   [세트]                                     (set grid, C14/C17)
#   +-----+---------+------+-----+-----+       (WT col FIXED 9 dashes -- C17)
#   | SET |    WT   | REPS | RIR |  ST |
#   ...setting (set), warmup (w1/w2), working (1/2) ...
#   누적 <done_vol>kg · <done>/<total>세트
#   휴식: <minutes>분 [<seconds>초]
#
#   ◂ <prev slot display>                      (footer, omitted if first)
#   ▸ <next slot display>                      (omitted if last)
#
# The WHOLE POINT (B5/C2): every row -- ramp + done + planned -- is emitted
# from state (workout_sets DB + program.yaml), so a whole table or a planned/
# ramp row can never be silently dropped by hand-typing (3x recurrence). No
# number is invented: unresolved working loads remain explicit, while a
# seeded program load is used when the prescription has no current load.
#
# Usage:
#   set-table <session_id> <exercise_name> [--db PATH] [--program PATH]
#
# Reuse: rx-calc (service/health/rx-calc, no .py ext) is imported via importlib
# for its hand-rolled stdlib YAML loader (load_yaml) and authoritative rest
# resolver (resolve_rest_sec) -- rest is READ, never invented. rx-calc has a
